# AutoHotkey Development Rules

## 📚 RULE #0: Check Central Documentation First

**BEFORE making any changes, ALWAYS check:**

- **Central Docs:** `D:\Dev\repos\mcp-central-docs\`
- **Standards:** `mcp-central-docs/STANDARDS.md` - Documentation & testing standards
- **FastMCP Guide:** `mcp-central-docs/FASTMCP_2.12_MIGRATION.md` - Framework standards

---

## Rule #1: AutoHotkey v2 Syntax Only - NO v1 ALLOWED
- **MANDATORY**: All scriptlets MUST be written in AutoHotkey v2 syntax from the start
- **FORBIDDEN**: Never write v1 syntax and "fix later" - this creates technical debt
- **REQUIRED**: Use `#Requires AutoHotkey v2.0+` directive in every scriptlet
- **ENFORCED**: The linter will catch and flag any v1 incompatibilities

### When Writing New Scripts:
- **ALWAYS write v2 syntax from the start** - DO NOT write v1 and convert
- **If unsure about v2 syntax:** Consult `docs/Complete_V1_to_V2_Migration_Guide.md`
- **If still unsure:** Check the official AutoHotkey v2 documentation in `AutoHotkeyDocs` repository
- **User instruction format:** When user says "write a new script that does X. use ahk v2 syntax only, no v1 syntax allowed. if in doubt, consult standards doc" - follow this exactly

## AutoHotkey v2 Syntax Requirements

### Function Calls
```autohotkey
# CORRECT v2:
FormatTime(timestamp, A_Now, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss")
FileRead(content, "file.txt")
MsgBox("Message", "Title", "0x30")
StrUpper(text)  ; Convert to uppercase
StrLower(text)  ; Convert to lowercase

# WRONG v1 (FORBIDDEN):
FormatTime timestamp,, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"
FileRead fileContent, fileToCheck
MsgBox, 0x30, Title, Message
text.ToUpper()  ; DOES NOT EXIST in v2!
text.ToLower()  ; DOES NOT EXIST in v2!
```

### Hotkeys
```autohotkey
# CORRECT v2:
Hotkey("^!c", (*) => Function())
Hotkey("F7", (*) => ClassName.Method())

# WRONG v1 (FORBIDDEN):
^!c::Function()
F7::ClassName.Method()
```

### For Loops
```autohotkey
# CORRECT v2:
for i := 1 .. 10
for i := array.Length .. 1
for item in array

# WRONG v1 (FORBIDDEN):
for i := 1 to 10
Loop, 10
```

### Random Function
```autohotkey
# CORRECT v2:
Random(value, 1, 100)
Random(direction, 0, 1)

# WRONG v1 (FORBIDDEN):
value := Random(1, 100)
Random(min, max)
```

### Variable Declarations
```autohotkey
# CORRECT v2:
var := "value"
static var := "value"
local var := "value"

# WRONG v1 (FORBIDDEN):
var = value
```

## Error Handling and Logging Requirements

### Mandatory Error Handling
Every scriptlet MUST include comprehensive error handling:

```autohotkey
# REQUIRED: Try-catch blocks for all file operations
try {
    FileRead(content, "file.txt")
} catch as e {
    this.AppendLog("File read error: " . e.Message)
    return false
}

# REQUIRED: Try-catch blocks for all GUI operations
try {
    this.gui.Show()
} catch as e {
    this.AppendLog("GUI error: " . e.Message)
}

# REQUIRED: Try-catch blocks for all system operations
try {
    Run("command.exe")
} catch as e {
    this.AppendLog("System command error: " . e.Message)
}
```

### Mandatory Logging System
Every scriptlet MUST implement a logging system:

```autohotkey
class ScriptletName {
    static logArea := ""
    
    static AppendLog(message) {
        timestamp := FormatTime(A_Now, "HH:mm:ss")
        logMessage := "[" . timestamp . "] " . message . "`n"
        
        if (this.logArea) {
            this.logArea.Text .= logMessage
            this.logArea.Focus()
            Send("^{End}")
        }
        
        ; Also log to file
        try {
            FileAppend(logMessage, "scriptlet.log", "UTF-8")
        } catch {
            ; Ignore file logging errors
        }
    }
}
```

## Code Quality Standards

### Class Structure Requirements
- **MANDATORY**: All scriptlets MUST use class-based structure
- **REQUIRED**: Include `static Init()` method
- **REQUIRED**: Include `static CreateGUI()` method for GUI scriptlets
- **REQUIRED**: Include `static AppendLog()` method for logging

### GUI Requirements
- **MANDATORY**: Use modern GUI syntax with proper event handling
- **REQUIRED**: Include error handling for all GUI operations
- **REQUIRED**: Include status bar or log area for user feedback

### Hotkey Requirements
- **MANDATORY**: Use `Hotkey()` function with proper syntax
- **REQUIRED**: Include `Escape` key to close GUI
- **REQUIRED**: Include emergency stop hotkey (`F9`) for infinite loops

## File Organization Standards

### Required Header
Every scriptlet MUST start with:
```autohotkey
#Requires AutoHotkey v2.0+
#SingleInstance Force

; ==============================================================================
; Scriptlet Name
; @name: Scriptlet Name
; @version: 1.0.0
; @description: Brief description
; @category: category
; @author: Sandra
; @hotkeys: ^!c, ^!v, ^!h
; @enabled: true
; ==============================================================================
```

### Required Footer
Every scriptlet MUST end with:
```autohotkey
; Initialize the scriptlet
ScriptletName.Init()
```

## Testing Requirements

### Pre-commit Testing
- **MANDATORY**: Run linter before committing any scriptlet
- **REQUIRED**: Fix ALL linter errors before submission
- **REQUIRED**: Test all hotkeys and GUI interactions
- **REQUIRED**: Verify error handling works correctly

### Linter Compliance
- **ZERO TOLERANCE**: No v1 syntax errors allowed
- **MANDATORY**: All FormatTime calls must have first parameter
- **MANDATORY**: All Random calls must use proper v2 syntax
- **MANDATORY**: All hotkeys must use Hotkey() function

## Performance Requirements

### Memory Management
- **REQUIRED**: Use `static` variables for class-wide data
- **REQUIRED**: Use `local` variables for function-scoped data
- **REQUIRED**: Clean up resources in error handlers

### Resource Cleanup
- **MANDATORY**: Close files and connections in error handlers
- **REQUIRED**: Clean up GUI resources on exit
- **REQUIRED**: Stop timers and monitoring on error

## Documentation Requirements

### Inline Comments
- **REQUIRED**: Comment all complex logic
- **REQUIRED**: Document all public methods
- **REQUIRED**: Explain error handling strategies

### User Documentation
- **REQUIRED**: Document all hotkeys in header
- **REQUIRED**: Include usage examples
- **REQUIRED**: Document error scenarios

## Enforcement

### Automated Checks
- **LINTER**: Will catch and flag ALL v1 incompatibilities
- **BUILD**: Will fail if any v1 syntax is detected
- **REVIEW**: Will reject any scriptlet with v1 syntax

### Manual Review
- **CODE REVIEW**: All scriptlets must pass manual review
- **TESTING**: All scriptlets must be tested before deployment
- **DOCUMENTATION**: All scriptlets must have proper documentation

## Examples of FORBIDDEN Patterns

```autohotkey
# NEVER DO THESE (v1 syntax):
FormatTime timestamp,, "format"
FileRead content, file
MsgBox, 0x30, Title, Message
^!c::Function()
for i := 1 to 10
value := Random(1, 100)
var = value
```

## Examples of REQUIRED Patterns

```autohotkey
# ALWAYS DO THESE (v2 syntax):
FormatTime(timestamp, A_Now, "format")
content := FileRead("file")
MsgBox("Message", "Title", "0x30")
Hotkey("^!c", (*) => Function())
for i := 1 .. 10
Random(value, 1, 100)
var := "value"
```

## Debugging and Running Requirements

### MANDATORY: Use /ErrorStdOut for ALL AutoHotkey executions
- **CRITICAL**: ALWAYS run AutoHotkey scripts with `/ErrorStdOut` flag to suppress error popups
- **FORBIDDEN**: Running AutoHotkey without `/ErrorStdOut` is strictly prohibited
- **EXAMPLE**: `AutoHotkey.exe '/ErrorStdOut' script.ahk`
- **REASON**: Error popups block terminal output and make debugging impossible

### Error Output Format
```
CORRECT:
AutoHotkey.exe '/ErrorStdOut' script.ahk

WRONG (FORBIDDEN):
AutoHotkey.exe script.ahk
```

### When Testing/Running Scriptlets
- **MANDATORY**: Always use `/ErrorStdOut` when running any `.ahk` file
- **REQUIRED**: Use full absolute paths to avoid file not found errors
- **REQUIRED**: Always check file exists before running
- **ENFORCED**: Running without `/ErrorStdOut` is considered a critical error

## MANDATORY V2 COMPLIANCE CHECKLIST

Before writing ANY code, AI must verify:
1. ✅ Is using modern v2 syntax (not v1 leftovers)
2. ✅ Using StrUpper() not .ToUpper()
3. ✅ Using StrLower() not .ToLower()
4. ✅ Using FormatTime(OUTPUT, INPUT, FORMAT) not FormatTime OUTPUT,,FORMAT
5. ✅ Using MsgBox("text", "title", "flags") not MsgBox, flags, title, text
6. ✅ Using Gui() not Gui, Add
7. ✅ Using Hotkey() function not ^!c:: syntax
8. ✅ All function calls use parentheses
9. ✅ No comma-separated command syntax
10. ✅ Using for i in array not Loop Array or for i := 1 to 10

## STRICT PROHIBITIONS

❌ NEVER use: FormatTime output,, format  (missing parentheses and commas)
❌ NEVER use: MsgBox, flags, title, text  (comma syntax)
❌ NEVER use: FileRead var, file  (comma syntax)
❌ NEVER use: StringReplace, StringSplit, StringLen  (use StrReplace, StrSplit, StrLen)
❌ NEVER use: Gui, Add (v1 command syntax)
❌ NEVER use: ^!c::  (v1 hotkey syntax)
❌ NEVER use: for i := 1 to 10  (use for i in Range(1, 10))
❌ NEVER use: .ToUpper() or .ToLower() methods
❌ NEVER use: Random(min, max) - must be Random(OUTPUT, min, max)
❌ NEVER use: any v1 syntax patterns

## Summary

**Rule #1: Write scriptlets in v2 syntax from the start. NO v1 allowed.**
**Rule #2: Include comprehensive error handling and logging.**
**Rule #3: Follow all code quality and testing requirements.**
**Rule #4: ALWAYS use /ErrorStdOut when running AutoHotkey scripts.**
**Rule #5: Use StrUpper() and StrLower(), NOT .ToUpper() or .ToLower() methods.**
**Rule #6: RUN LINTER after every scriptlet creation to catch v1 syntax.**
**Rule #7: When a bug, syntax violation, or bad pattern is discovered in one scriptlet, immediately search the entire repository for the same pattern and remediate every occurrence in the same sweep. Never leave the same fix to be rediscovered in other files.**

Any violation of these rules will result in immediate rejection of the scriptlet.
